Independent light runtime: disconnected-load first installation

Target: Raspberry Pi 4 Model B Rev 1.1, aarch64, Python3.13, gpiochip0/21.
Run from a new root-owned private directory at the trusted root@DietPi console.
Verify the archive and manifest hashes supplied with this package before use.

python3 -I -B install_light.py --valves-disconnected --lamp-disconnected --manifest-sha256 <pinned SHA256>

Only newly created light services and HTTPS camera route8443 are installed.
The shower environment, paired daemon, GPIO20/26 and Node-RED are preserved.
All dependencies are offline and hash pinned in an isolated light-only venv.
The initial light state must be OFF. No ON command is sent by the installer.
The root-only evidence directory records a private baseline backup and receipt.
On failure preserve the directory and marker; do not rerun or delete them.

Accepted limitation: executor crash/hang may leave the light ON indefinitely.
Systemd restart is operational recovery, not a guaranteed physical cutoff.
The original LIGHT_LEVEL_MISMATCH bench result remains unchanged. Both loads
must stay disconnected until separate physical acceptance. GPIO readback does
not prove relay contact position or suitability of mains wiring.

Camera forwarding remains unconfigured. A new camera token is generated onPi
and exported only encrypted to the VM recipient public key under
<evidence>/backup/provisioning/camera-token.enc. The accompanying server.crt
is the public trust anchor for the new HTTPS endpoint. The token, endpoint
and certificate SHA256 are inside the encrypted payload. No token is printed.
The display/settings credentials remain root-only onPi for later provisioning.

This is a first-install tool: an existing light account, units, target paths,
or attempt marker require review. It provides no automatic rollback/retry.
